    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93006" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάγᾰρις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>
		
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἡ</span>; pl.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαγάρεις</span>
		
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῑς</span>:—a weapon used by the
		Scythian tribes, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.215
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			4.5
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀξίνας σαγάρις εἶχον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.64
				</span></i>
			; by the Amazons, <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PAmh.</u>
				2.12
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				 ii 10
			</span></i>; by the Persians, Amazons, Mossynoeci, etc., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.4.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.4.13
			</span></i>:—acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> single-edged, and joined by <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i> with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπίς</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχαιρα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.1.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.2.22
			</span></i>; double-edged acc. to <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.94
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>).</div>
